          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Warren A. Wolf, the case concerns whether ineffective assistance of counsel claims can be raised on direct appeal in Texas, or must be brought in state habeas proceedings."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Warren A. Wolf",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Warren A. Wolf, texas operates a dual\u2011track system, created in 1995, to expedite certain claims\u2014especially death\u2011penalty claims\u2014through a separate habeas\u2011style route."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Warren A. Wolf",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0eedf2219cbdf1f2bc7cc94c98dad9a49a9852f6a2794414539ba66bcf2b3727",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0eedf2219cbd-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Warren A. Wolf, the Texas Court of Criminal Appeals has repeatedly held that defendants should not raise ineffective assistance of counsel claims on direct appeal, making such claims effectively unavailable on that track."
      }
    ],
